            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-text-muted-light mt-3 italic text-center">
            Every season offers something. Evergreens keep releasing phytoncides straight through the winter.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
        <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.5rem] font-medium lg:text-3xl lg:font-medium text-text-main-light pt-4" id="common-mistakes">
          Common Mistakes to Avoid
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 size-6 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">✗</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main-light">Treating It Like Exercise</span>
              <p class="text-base text-text-muted-light">Don't approach with a fitness mentality. Shinrin-Yoku is about being, not doing. It's therapy, not a workout.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 size-6 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">✗</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main-light">Staying in Your Head</span>
              <p class="text-base text-text-muted-light">If you spend your visit mentally planning or worrying, you're not truly practicing. The benefits come from sensory engagement and present-moment awareness.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 size-6 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">✗</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main-light">Rushing Through It</span>
              <p class="text-base text-text-muted-light">Walk slower than feels natural. If you catch yourself speeding up, pause and take three deep breaths before continuing.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-4">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 size-6 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-600 flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold mt-1">✗</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-lg font-bold text-text-main-light">Giving Up Too Soon</span>
              <p class="text-base text-text-muted-light">Commit to trying forest bathing 1-2 times weekly for at least a month before deciding if it works for you.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <!-- FAQ Section -->
        <h2 class="font-serif text-[1.5rem] font-medium lg:text-3xl lg:font-medium text-text-main-light pt-4" id="faq">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4 my-8">
          <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden group">
            <summary class="p-5 cursor-pointer font-bold text-text-main-light flex justify-between items-center">
              Do I need an actual forest, or will a park work?
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-accent-dark group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-base text-text-muted-light">
              Any space with substantial tree coverage works. Urban parks, botanical gardens, or even tree-filled neighborhoods can offer benefits. The key is having enough trees to create a canopy and the sense of being in nature.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden group">
            <summary class="p-5 cursor-pointer font-bold text-text-main-light flex justify-between items-center">
              How long before I notice benefits?
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-accent-dark group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-base text-text-muted-light">
              Many people report immediate effects like improved mood after a single session. For measurable physiological changes like immune boosting, expect benefits to accumulate with regular practice over 2-4 weeks.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden group">
            <summary class="p-5 cursor-pointer font-bold text-text-main-light flex justify-between items-center">
              Is Shinrin-Yoku safe for seniors with health conditions?
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-accent-dark group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-base text-text-muted-light">
              Shinrin-Yoku is generally very safe as it involves gentle activity. Still, always consult your doctor before starting any new health practice, especially if you have heart conditions or mobility challenges. Most healthcare providers view it as beneficial complementary therapy.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden group">
            <summary class="p-5 cursor-pointer font-bold text-text-main-light flex justify-between items-center">
              What if I have allergies to trees or pollen?
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-accent-dark group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-base text-text-muted-light">
              You can practice during seasons when your allergens are less active, or in locations with trees that don't trigger your allergies (evergreens vs. deciduous). Taking allergy medication beforehand is fine, and the other benefits still apply.
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 overflow-hidden group">
            <summary class="p-5 cursor-pointer font-bold text-text-main-light flex justify-between items-center">
              Can I practice Shinrin-Yoku every day?
              <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-accent-dark group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">expand_more</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-base text-text-muted-light">
              Absolutely! Daily practice would provide maximum benefits. Many people in Japan practice daily, though even 1-2 times weekly offers significant health improvements.
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>

